sequenceDiagram
    participant App as App<br>[implements GapCentralResponse]
    participant Node as Node<br>[implements GapCentral]

    Note over App, Node: Allowed states: standby.<br>Calling outside standby asserts on the Node.<br>Fire-and-forget, no response callback.<br>Should be called once during initialization<br>before any connections are made.

    App->>Node: GapCentral.SetSecurityMode(<br>mode=mode1, level=authenticatedPairing)

    Note over App: If the connected peripheral does not meet the required level,<br>PairAndBond fails with reason=authenticationRequirementsNotMet.<br>The link stays connected on SMP failure. The App must call Standby<br>(or wait for the peer to disconnect) to reach CurrentState(standby).<br>The Connect procedure itself is unaffected: the link reaches<br>CurrentState(connected) regardless of capability match.<br>Security mode is a pairing-time requirement, not a Connect-time filter.
